# LoC MARC country code → YSO bridge with multilingual labels.
#
# Per docs/bffi_limitations.md L-12, neither LoC's countries vocabulary
# nor YSO publishes a cross-reference between
# <http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/countries/{code}> and the corresponding
# YSO concept. This file is our own bridge: one skos:exactMatch into
# main YSO plus inlined fi/sv/en prefLabels (cached from YSO at the
# time this file was written, so it stays useful even when Fuseki is
# offline at Skosify time).
#
# Source: LoC MARC country code list (https://www.loc.gov/marc/countries/cou_home.html)
# and YSO / YSO-paikat.
#
# License: CC0 (project bridge; YSO labels are Finto-curated CC0).

@prefix bridge: <http://urn.fi/URN:NBN:fi:bib:bridge/loc-countries/> .
@prefix loc:    <http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/countries/> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix yso:    <http://www.yso.fi/onto/yso/> .

# === Bridge graph identifier ===

bridge: a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "Local LoC MARC country code ↔ YSO bridge"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Project-owned bridge — see docs/bffi_limitations.md L-12."@en .

